WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.831 --> 00:00:04.511
The new filling unit on line 3 in hall B is ready.

2
00:00:05.188 --> 00:00:07.661
It fills cartons with product from the tank.

3
00:00:08.727 --> 00:00:13.499
The new MES from the IT team sends it orders and gets counts back.

4
00:00:14.557 --> 00:00:15.776
You are the engineer.

5
00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:18.683
You connect the unit step by step.

6
00:00:19.703 --> 00:00:21.421
That makes five stations.

7
00:00:22.148 --> 00:00:26.293
From network and OT to security, the line itself and data.

8
00:00:27.755 --> 00:00:30.483
The first station is IT fundamentals.

9
00:00:31.205 --> 00:00:35.977
The unit’s control cabinet has to join the plant network via the network cabinet.

10
00:00:37.055 --> 00:00:40.073
Every device has an address, like a house number.

11
00:00:40.822 --> 00:00:42.633
Messages go to that address.

12
00:00:43.637 --> 00:00:45.518
You use a switch and a VLAN.

13
00:00:46.521 --> 00:00:48.971
Without this an order does not find the unit,

14
00:00:49.145 --> 00:00:51.444
or the line sits on the office network.

15
00:00:52.770 --> 00:00:56.346
The second station is IT and OT on the shop floor.

16
00:00:57.071 --> 00:01:00.577
The PLC in the control cabinet controls the unit.

17
00:01:01.626 --> 00:01:03.693
Orders go down to the PLC.

18
00:01:04.360 --> 00:01:07.019
Confirmations go up to the MES.

19
00:01:08.054 --> 00:01:10.748
You set up an OPC server and tags.

20
00:01:11.780 --> 00:01:15.321
Without this the MES does not know what the line makes.

21
00:01:16.624 --> 00:01:19.004
The third station is Cybersecurity.

22
00:01:19.703 --> 00:01:22.524
An attack on the office must not stop line 3.

23
00:01:23.551 --> 00:01:27.405
Line 3 gets its own zone, with one guarded link to the rest.

24
00:01:28.548 --> 00:01:30.858
You define zones and conduits.

25
00:01:31.872 --> 00:01:35.239
Without this an infection from the office can stop the line.

26
00:01:36.509 --> 00:01:39.191
The fourth station is Lines and automation.

27
00:01:39.926 --> 00:01:43.641
That is the line itself, where cartons arrive and get filled.

28
00:01:44.701 --> 00:01:48.648
The unit may only fill when a sensor sees a carton under the plate.

29
00:01:49.726 --> 00:01:51.978
You use poka-yoke and an interlock.

30
00:01:53.062 --> 00:01:56.638
Without this product runs onto the belt when no carton is there.

31
00:01:57.951 --> 00:02:01.480
The fifth station is Data and digital manufacturing.

32
00:02:02.191 --> 00:02:05.175
What line 3 makes has to be visible on the floor.

33
00:02:06.185 --> 00:02:10.411
The unit’s numbers go to the MES and to a screen by the line.

34
00:02:11.384 --> 00:02:13.787
You use an edge gateway and a dashboard.

35
00:02:14.852 --> 00:02:17.941
Without this the numbers come too late, or they are wrong.

36
00:02:19.241 --> 00:02:20.449
This is the whole map.

37
00:02:21.171 --> 00:02:25.200
The five stations of Automation and IT lie in one zone.

38
00:02:26.195 --> 00:02:31.199
First IT fundamentals, from networks and cloud to databases and software.

39
00:02:32.282 --> 00:02:37.147
Then IT and OT on the shop floor, from ISA-95 to who owns what.

40
00:02:38.270 --> 00:02:42.670
Then Cybersecurity, from the basics to the law and incident response.

41
00:02:43.731 --> 00:02:48.537
Then Lines and automation, with robots, error-proofing and the business case.

42
00:02:49.540 --> 00:02:54.022
Finally Data and digital manufacturing, from data quality to AI.

43
00:02:55.065 --> 00:02:56.447
That is how they connect.

44
00:02:57.171 --> 00:03:02.186
The network joins the systems, and the line talks over it with the MES.

45
00:03:03.199 --> 00:03:05.126
Cybersecurity guards that link.

46
00:03:05.863 --> 00:03:09.463
The line makes the products, and data shows how it goes.

47
00:03:10.502 --> 00:03:13.602
Each station is a module with four levels per topic.

48
00:03:14.390 --> 00:03:16.433
Start with what your line needs now.
